WEBVTT

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:04.550
We'll be right back.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.430
Yeah, boss, right away, boss.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:30.000
You're supposed to knock out the United States by this time.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.260
Uh, but boss, we're building up our strength, we're...

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:34.940
Yeah, but you're moving too slow.

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.630
Uh, what do we do?

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:42.350
You and your communist pals keep trouble brewing in Asia and Europe.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.400
I'll go to work on the USA from the inside.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.240
You're gonna plant an atom bomb, boys?

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.800
Oh boy, oh boy!

00:01:53.240 --> 00:02:00.000
The seeds I've planted in the United States are far more deadly than atom bombs.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:37.790
John Q. Inflation, don't worry me, nuns, so long the government keeps farm prices high and subsidies high.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.130
Inflation is everybody's problem.

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:45.760
Not with us farmers, by cracky. We're making twice the money we used to.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:51.200
What's the good of having twice as many dollars if you have to pay three times as much for what you buy?

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:56.060
So, you reactionary city slickers just want to see us farmers go broke?

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.580
That burns me up!

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:06.410
Now, John Q, business should raise prices to keep profit ratios in line.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:12.870
If business gouges labor with unnecessary high prices, that only feeds the fires of inflation.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:22.850
Oh, now, John Q, if we businessmen stick together, we can keep profits high and keep labor right under our thumb.

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:29.110
Well, if high prices make it impossible for the people to buy the goods that industry produces, everybody suffers.

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:30.000
Why, you crazy!

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.990
Crackpot liberal, let me tell you something!

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:42.930
Well, John Q, seems like the old paycheck buys less every day.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:47.530
Yeah, I have to dig into my savings most every week to keep up with inflation.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:50.070
Inflation can't hurt us union boys.

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:53.720
If wages don't keep ahead of prices, we'll strike.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.910
Generally, if wages go up, so do prices.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:57.920
Get him!

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.000
Anti-labor if I ever heard one!

